{{Infobox item
| Name = {{{1}}} Berrynana Peel
| Title = {{{1}}} Berrynana Peel
| images = {{{1}}} Berrynana Peel.png {{#if: {{{nocb|}}} ||, {{{1}}} Berrynana Peel CB.png}}
| tabs = {{#if: {{{nocb|}}} || Normal, Colorblind }}
| Biome = Tropics
| Weight = 2.5
| Source = {{{1}}} Berrynana
}}

The '''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[item]] in {{peak game}} that is acquired after eating {{item|{{{1}}} Berrynana}}s from the [[Tropics]]. Players walking over a peel will [[Slippery effect|slip]] and fall to the ground, losing control for a moment. 

== Notes ==
* After eating a {{Item|{{{1}}} Berrynana}}, the resulting peel behaves differently depending on the type of game session:
** In a multiplayer session, the {{PAGENAME}} will appear in the player's inventory if there's space; if there is no space it will drop at their feet resulting in an immediate slip when they move.
** In a single-player sessions, the peel will always drop at the player's feet resulting in an immediate slip when they move.

== Patch history ==
{{patch|1.0|Introduced.}}

== Usage ==

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
{{Badges|list of badges|size=48px|perRow=24}}
</syntaxhighlight>

{{Badges|size=48px|perRow=24}}

=== Example ===

==== Default by Negating ====

The following syntax will show all badges ''except'' for the ones that are removed with '-'. Can be used to negate all badges that are still locked and then removed as they're unlocked. Rather than needing to add the ones that ''are'' unlocked.

{{#tag:syntaxhighlight|<nowiki>{{Badges|</nowiki>{{#invoke:Badges|all|1}}<nowiki>}}</nowiki>|lang=mediawiki}}

==== Default by Boolean ====

The following syntax will show all badges that have a ''truthy'' value, and not the ones that don't. Badges that are locked are represented with a ':0' and can be changed to a ':1' after they ''are'' unlocked. Useful if you want to list all badges regardless of locked or unlocked.

{{#tag:syntaxhighlight|<nowiki>{{Badges|</nowiki>{{#invoke:Badges|all|2}}<nowiki>}}</nowiki>|lang=mediawiki}}

==== All badges ====

The ''all'' input can be used if you want to show all badges as unlocked, without having to list any of them.

<syntaxhighlight lang="mediawiki">{{Badges|all|perRow=24}}</syntaxhighlight>

{{Badges|all|perRow=24}}

{{No direct use}}

